## 5. Registers

"Register" means two different things. Keep them separate.

### 5.1 CPU core registers (Cortex-M)

| Register | Role |
|---|---|
| R0–R12 | General purpose (R0–R7 reachable by all Thumb instructions) |
| R13 (SP) | Stack pointer (MSP main / PSP process) |
| R14 (LR) | Link register: return address |
| R15 (PC) | Program counter |
| xPSR | Status flags and execution state |

### 5.2 Peripheral registers

These are **memory-mapped hardware registers** that control peripherals (e.g. GPIO mode, UART data). They live at fixed addresses in the memory map and are accessed like variables.

