## Lab: Inspect Your Own Memory Layout

Build the LED example (or any blink project) and then:

1. Run `arm-none-eabi-size` on the ELF file. Record `text`, `data` and `bss`.
2. Run `arm-none-eabi-objdump -h` and note each section's **VMA** (runtime address) and **LMA** (load address). Explain why `.data` has different values for each.
3. Open the linker script and find the `MEMORY` block. Match the flash and RAM origins and lengths to the table in 6.2.
4. Add a `const` array and a non-`const` array of the same size. Re-run `size` and explain which section grew in each case.

